From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pyroshine Vendor Maintenance <vendor@pyroshine.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:19:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] av1: code the frame on the implementation's picture grid

Implementations code AV1 pictures on their codedPictureAlignment grid but
read the source image only within the picture resource's codedExtent and
fill the remainder themselves. With the requested size as codedExtent,
RADV (8x2 grid) coded a 1365x767 frame as 1368x768 whose last row was black
(Y=16), so decoders that ignore render_size showed a black line instead of
the caller's edge padding.

Use the requested size rounded up to the grid, within the coded extent,
as max_frame_* and every picture's codedExtent, and signal the requested
size with render_and_frame_size_different and render_size. Expose the
extent as EncoderCapabilities::av1_frame_extent.
---
 src/encoder/av1/init.rs           |  4 +++
 src/encoder/av1/mod.rs            |  3 ++
 src/encoder/av1/record.rs         | 13 +++++---
 src/encoder/av1/session_params.rs |  4 +--
 src/encoder/capabilities.rs       | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

